{"page": 1, "segments": [{"index": 0, "text": "Steps: (1) x.next = y.next (2) x.prev = y (3) if y.next \u2260 NIL: y.next.prev = x (4) y.next = x ##### LIST-DELETE(L, x) \u2014 O(1) given\npointer\nSteps: (1) if x.prev \u2260 NIL: x.prev.next = x.next (2) else L.head = x.next (3) if x.next \u2260 NIL: x.next.prev = x.prev ##### LIST-\nDELETE\u2019(x) \u2014 with sentinel, O(1)\nSteps: (1) x.prev.next = x.next (2) x.next.prev = x.prev \u2014 no boundary checks needed ##### LIST-SEARCH\u2019(L, k) \u2014 sentinel\noptimization\nSteps: (1) L.nil.key = k (guarantees key somewhere) (2) x = L.nil.next (3) while x.key \u2260 k: x = x.next (4) if x == L.nil: return NIL (5)\nelse return x\nAdvantage: Only 1 comparison per iteration vs 2 standard.", "rects": [[37.411865234375, 10.210999488830566, 559.0014038085938, 22.953899383544922], [37.411865234375, 23.46563720703125, 65.57791137695312, 36.13477325439453], [37.411865234375, 36.72027587890625, 534.1368408203125, 49.46317672729492], [37.411865234375, 49.97491455078125, 174.6045684814453, 62.64405059814453], [37.411865234375, 63.22955322265625, 549.4295043945312, 75.97245788574219], [37.411865234375, 76.4842529296875, 86.56159973144531, 89.15338897705078], [37.411865234375, 89.7388916015625, 562.2939453125, 102.48179626464844], [37.411865234375, 102.9935302734375, 88.08927154541016, 115.66266632080078], [37.411865234375, 116.2481689453125, 278.02752685546875, 128.99107360839844]], "duration": 65.225, "start_time": 0.0, "end_time": 65.225}, {"index": 1, "text": "Guarantee of finding key in list (possibly sentinel).", "rects": [[280.5787658691406, 116.2481689453125, 483.3214416503906, 128.9173126220703]], "duration": 3.85, "start_time": 65.225, "end_time": 69.07499999999999}, {"index": 2, "text": "#####\nTRANSPLANT(T, u, v) \u2014 BST utility\nSteps: (1) if u.p == NIL: T.root = v (2) else if u == u.p.left: u.p.left = v (3) else u.p.right = v (4) if v \u2260 NIL: v.p = u.p ##### COMPACT-\nLIST-SEARCH (Problem 10-3) \u2014 randomized, expected O(\u221an)\nIdea: While scanning forward in sorted compact list, periodically pick random index j.", "rects": [[485.8726806640625, 116.2481689453125, 511.4936218261719, 128.9173126220703], [37.411865234375, 129.5028076171875, 185.86927795410156, 142.1719512939453], [37.411865234375, 142.7574462890625, 572.8021850585938, 155.50035095214844], [37.411865234375, 156.0120849609375, 292.4376220703125, 168.6812286376953], [37.411865234375, 169.2667236328125, 381.43536376953125, 182.00962829589844]], "duration": 31.45, "start_time": 69.07499999999999, "end_time": 100.52499999999999}, {"index": 3, "text": "If key[j] is between current key[i] and target k,\njump to j. ALGORITHM: i=head; while i\u2260NIL and key[i]<k { j=RANDOM(1,n); if key[i]<key[j]\u2264k: i=j; if key[i]==k: return i; i=next[i] }; return NIL if\nnot found. Analysis via COMPACT-LIST-SEARCH\u2019: Two-phase: t random skips then linear scan.", "rects": [[383.9866027832031, 169.2667236328125, 568.8013305664062, 181.9358673095703], [37.411865234375, 182.5213623046875, 74.77764129638672, 195.1905059814453], [37.411865234375, 195.7760009765625, 567.6397094726562, 208.51890563964844], [37.411865234375, 209.03070068359375, 78.3884506225586, 221.69984436035156], [37.411865234375, 222.28533935546875, 393.2132568359375, 235.0282440185547]], "duration": 26.925, "start_time": 100.52499999999999, "end_time": 127.44999999999999}, {"index": 4, "text": "Expected O(t + n/(t+1)). Choose t=\u221an \u2192\nO(\u221an). Assumption: All keys distinct. Repeated keys break: random skips may bypass equal keys that should match. Example: n=100, sorted compact list. t=10 skips expected skip ~91% of distance, leaving ~10 elements to scan linearly.", "rects": [[395.7644958496094, 222.28533935546875, 558.404052734375, 234.95448303222656], [37.411865234375, 235.53997802734375, 62.55851745605469, 248.20912170410156], [37.411865234375, 248.79461669921875, 486.96826171875, 261.5375061035156], [37.411865234375, 262.04925537109375, 526.4530639648438, 274.7921447753906]], "duration": 24.675, "start_time": 127.44999999999999, "end_time": 152.125}, {"index": 5, "text": "Classifications & Hierarchies", "rects": [[14.360311508178711, 287.4520568847656, 141.3180389404297, 300.1488342285156]], "duration": 2.55, "start_time": 152.125, "end_time": 154.675}, {"index": 6, "text": "Linked list variants:", "rects": [[37.411865234375, 313.33892822265625, 123.40201568603516, 326.0818176269531]], "duration": 1.85, "start_time": 154.675, "end_time": 156.525}, {"index": 7, "text": "Singly linked (next only) vs. Doubly linked (next + prev) vs. XOR linked (np = next XOR prev)\nSorted (by key) vs. Unsorted\nCircular (tail.next = head) vs. Non-circular\nMatrix storage: Single-array (row-major, column-major) vs. Multiple-array (ragged arrays) vs.", "rects": [[60.46342086791992, 326.59356689453125, 437.7974853515625, 339.2626953125], [60.46342086791992, 339.84820556640625, 177.19203186035156, 352.517333984375], [60.46342086791992, 353.10284423828125, 230.1444091796875, 365.77197265625], [37.411865234375, 366.35748291015625, 418.1467590332031, 379.1003723144531]], "duration": 22.175, "start_time": 156.525, "end_time": 178.70000000000002}, {"index": 8, "text": "Block representation\nTree representation: Binary (p,left,right) vs. Left-child/right-sibling vs. Array-only (heaps, Ch6) vs. Parent-only (disjoint sets, Ch19)\nStack/Queue implementation: Array-based (fixed size, wraparound) vs. Linked-list-based (dynamic size)", "rects": [[420.697998046875, 366.35748291015625, 504.6772155761719, 379.026611328125], [37.411865234375, 379.61212158203125, 570.262939453125, 392.3550109863281], [37.411865234375, 392.86688232421875, 468.4398498535156, 405.6097717285156]], "duration": 20.55, "start_time": 178.70000000000002, "end_time": 199.25000000000003}, {"index": 9, "text": "Comparisons & Trade-offs", "rects": [[14.360311508178711, 418.2696838378906, 130.02638244628906, 430.9664611816406]], "duration": 2.1, "start_time": 199.250